                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">CORTISOL — A CLASSIC HORMONE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Source, action, and regulation</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">SOURCE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Adrenal cortex — zona fasciculata</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"315\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Synthesized from cholesterol (steroid hormone)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Released under ACTH from anterior pituitary</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"390\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">ACTIONS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"495\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Gluconeogenesis from amino acids</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"535\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Protein catabolism + lipolysis</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"575\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Anti-inflammatory; immune suppression</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"610\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"665\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">REGULATION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"715\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Hypothalamus CRH → pituitary ACTH → cortisol</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cortisol negatively feeds back at both</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Diurnal rhythm — highest in morning</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"830\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"885\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">SOURCE-ACTION-REGULATION TRIO</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Master this for every major hormone</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Cortisol: cortex → gluconeogenesis → negative feedback on ACTH."
